---
title: Mushroom Risotto
cooklang: 2
servings: 4
unit system: metric
course: dinner
cuisine: Italian
time:
  prep: 20 minutes
  cook: 45 minutes
techniques: [soak, sweat, toast, deglaze, beat in]
tags: [rice, one pan, stress test]
---

= Stock -> hot stock

`Soak` @dried porcini{20%g} in @-hot water{250%ml} in a #small bowl{} for ~{20%minutes}.
-> soaked porcini + soaking liquid{200%ml}

`Strain` the @&soaking liquid{} through a #fine sieve{} into a #saucepan{}, leaving the
grit behind.

`Add` @./Bases/Chicken Stock{1%l}|@vegetable stock{1%l}?vegetarian and a
@parmesan rind{30%g}. `Keep bare simmer low` at a bare simmer over low heat.

= Risotto -> risotto

`Sweat medium-low` @shallots{2}(finely chopped) in @olive oil{2%tbsp} and @butter{20%g} in a
#wide heavy pan{} over medium-low heat for ~{5%minutes} until ~{soft but not coloured}.

`Fry medium-high` @chestnut mushrooms{300%g}(sliced) and the @&soaked porcini{}(squeezed, chopped) in
the #&wide heavy pan{} over medium-high heat for ~{6%minutes} until ~{their liquid has evaporated and they begin to brown}.

`Toast` @arborio rice{320%g}, stirring, for ~{2%minutes} until ~{the edges turn translucent}.

`Deglaze` with @dry white wine{150%ml}, stirring until ~{it has evaporated}.

`Discard` the @&parmesan rind{} from the stock.

`Add medium ×` the @&hot stock{1%ladle} at a time over medium heat, stirring until ~{each ladle is absorbed before the next}, for ~{18%minutes} until ~{the rice is tender with a slight bite}.

`Beat in off` @&butter{30%g}(cold, cubed) and @parmesan{60%g}(finely grated) off the heat for
~{1%minute} until ~{creamy}. `Season` with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

`Rest covered` covered for ~rest{2%minutes}. `Serve` with @?flat-leaf parsley{}(chopped).
